Real progress to register first: the theme-grouping bug from before is fixed. Theme 1 and Theme 2 now correctly split 3/3 instead of all 6 landing under Theme 1, and — importantly — the UI and the backend log now agree with each other. That mismatch was the whole reason we couldn't trust "looks fine in the diagnosis script" before; now what you see in the browser matches what's actually happening server-side.

But this run surfaces a new, different problem — and the timing in the log is the interesting part:

02:37:57 → Theme 1 call starts (fetches a fresh auth token first)
02:39:33 → Theme 1 finishes: 27,848 chars, full real content, 96 seconds elapsed
02:39:33 → Theme 2 call starts immediately after
02:39:41 → Theme 2 finishes: "Answer 0 chars" — 8 seconds elapsed

Theme 1 took 96 seconds and returned a fully-populated, real answer. Theme 2, run back-to-back right after, took 8 seconds and came back completely empty. That gap is the tell: a search that genuinely looked and found nothing would still take real time to search — 8 seconds returning zero characters looks much more like the call got refused or cut short than like "we searched and there's no data." That's consistent with the UI: Theme 2's three events all show the amber "No results — try re-scanning" state, matching the backend's [WARNING] Empty answer for theme: Global Monetary Policy.

This is worth treating as its own distinct bug, separate from everything before it. Two candidate explanations, and the fix differs depending on which:

Rate limiting / throttling on back-to-back calls — if so, this isn't a "Global Monetary Policy" problem at all, it's a "second call in quick succession" problem, and it'll happen to whichever theme happens to run second.
Something specific to how that theme's query resolves — less likely given the instant failure, but worth ruling out.

The fast way to tell them apart: re-run the scan with the theme order swapped (Global Monetary Policy first, US Trade Policy & Tariffs second). If the first theme now succeeds and the second one fails empty regardless of which theme it is, that confirms it's a rate-limit/throttling issue on consecutive calls — not anything about that specific theme's content.

Send Stylus this, with the actual log lines attached:

"Theme 1 succeeded (96s, 27,848 chars). Theme 2, called immediately after, returned 0 chars in 8 seconds. Is there a rate limit or cooldown on back-to-back web_search_agent calls? Check whether the exception handling around that call could be silently swallowing an error and returning empty string instead of raising."

And don't let this new finding bump the Gemini/Claude question off the list — that's still sitting open from last message, unrelated to this bug, and this run doesn't tell us anything new about it either way.



